# Separate browser website sessions from API and OAuth access

- Consumer Safari/Chrome login DOES NOT give Blossom an OpenAI API key, Spotify Web API token, Suno Platform account, or ChatGPT MCP installation.
- Never automate Google SSO in Playwright/stealth WebDriver, copy Safari cookies, spoof bot flags, or use private website endpoints as an unofficial API.
- Open official login URLs in a normal native user browser; browser session reuse remains controlled by that browser.
- Spotify Facebook login is only usable if supported by the existing account. Distinguish initial sign-in from Spotify Web Player.
- A Blossom user_confirmed handoff means manual confirmation, NOT a verified live provider session or API connection. Browser close/login cannot be detected reliably without callback.
- For background AI use an authorized developer API or a clearly labelled locally installed model; do not pretend that a ChatGPT website tab is a headless inference API.
- Never weaken allowed-provider URLs, CSRF checks or local-only browser launcher permissions.
